---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { publisherRef } from '../lib/schema';
import { site } from '../site';

const steps = [
  { name: 'Open the set', text: 'Start on a collection page if you want several pictures. Open one drawing if your child already picked a favorite.' },
  { name: 'Download the PDF', text: 'Choose US Letter for a standard American home printer, 8.5 by 11 inches. Choose A4 if the paper pack says A4.' },
  { name: 'Print at actual size', text: 'In the print dialog, choose actual size or 100%. If the printer warns that the page does not fit, switch to fit-to-page. Do not print the browser window.' },
  { name: 'Color', text: 'Crayons and colored pencils stay inside the lines on ordinary copy paper. Markers look brighter and bleed more; cardstock helps if you use them.' },
];
const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'HowTo',
  name: 'How to print a coloring page',
  description: 'Download a US Letter or A4 PDF and print it at actual size for kids to color.',
  inLanguage: site.locale,
  publisher: publisherRef(),
  step: steps.map((step, index) => ({
    '@type': 'HowToStep',
    position: index + 1,
    name: step.name,
    text: step.text,
  })),
};
---

<Base title="How to print coloring pages" description="How to download and print free coloring pages on US Letter or A4 paper, with crayon and classroom tips." path="/how-to-print/" jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <div class="wrap prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">Printing guide</p>
    <h1>How to print these coloring pages</h1>
    <p>The file you want is the PDF. A screenshot of the web page prints the menu, the ads, and a blurry drawing. The PDF is just the picture, with room for the paper margins.</p>
    {steps.map((step, index) => (
      <section>
        <h2>{index + 1}. {step.name}</h2>
        <p>{step.text}</p>
      </section>
    ))}
    <h2>Letter or A4</h2>
    <p>Most kitchens in the United States have US Letter paper. A4 is slightly taller and a little narrower. Each drawing is saved twice so the same picture sits properly on either sheet. If you are not sure, letter is the right first try on a printer bought in the US.</p>
    <h2>In a classroom</h2>
    <p>Teachers and caregivers can print a class set for free. Print the PDF once and copy it, or print the copies straight from the file. Please don't upload the PDF to a shop or sell the printed pages.</p>
    <h2>If the lines look faint</h2>
    <p>Choose black-and-white or the printer's "text" setting if a draft mode washes the lines out. The drawing is black ink on white, so color printing is not required.</p>
    <p>Questions about a file: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
